WEBVTT

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:04.150
Boy...

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.270
You've brought Cannon Gear down admirably.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.230
But...

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.820
it's still too early to feel at ease.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.890
Even after losing Cannon Gear, 
my army stands as firm as a rock!

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.130
Let's go to war, my strongest soldier!

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.290
Glorious mechanical dragon! 
Gallop across the Earth!

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.300
I ride...

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.920
Tyrant Deathrex!

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.260
Deathrex!

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.550
That's definitely a powerful unit...

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.420
But no matter how strong his units are...

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.570
I'm not gonna lose!

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.480
For Kamui's sake...

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.730
And for the sake of my other teammates...

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.950
I'm going to win this fight, no matter what!

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.720
The crowd is pumped up,

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.110
here at the Vanguard Fight A Block Hall!

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.600
And now, it's Ryudou's turn.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:41.720
He seems to be full of confidence, but 
what kind of attack will he show us?

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.520
The true fearsomeness 
of the Tachikaze deck...

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.470
If he is able to pull that off...

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.830
No ordinary Fighter could defend against it!

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.760
The outcome of the match could 
be determined this turn!

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:58.320
Dr. O, what is this "fearsomeness" 
of the Tachikaze deck?!

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.950
I call Raging Dragon Blastsaurus! Skyptero!

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.190
And Savage Destroyer!

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.130
Attention, all units! Prepare for attack!

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.250
Here it comes!

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:18.380
Be careful, Aichi!

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:26.640
Aggressive Advancement! Tachikaze Deck!

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.560
With a boost from Skyptero...

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.070
Blastsaurus attacks Blaster Blade!

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:38.360
I guard with Elaine!

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.820
I attack with Deathrex!

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:53.580
When Deathrex attacks, its 
power increases by 5000!

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.860
His power is 15000...

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.930
Twin drive, first check!

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.590
Second check!

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.280
Damage trigger check!

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.700
The success of my attack has been confirmed!

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.650
I activate Deathrex's skill!

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.900
One of my allies must leave the field!

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.110
Blastsaurus! Sacrifice yourself!

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.820
This unit's skill also activates 
by sacrificing an ally...

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:28.740
It's not just any old sacrifice!

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.340
It's a sacrifice that paves the way!

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.890
Wounded, fallen Blastsaurus!

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:38.040
Show me your skill!

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:43.520
When this soldier is placed in the drop 
zone, if I discard one unit from my hand...

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.160
I can call a new Blastsaurus!

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.780
A new Blastsaurus?!

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:52.280
Then he can attack one more time!

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.760
That's not all!

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.930
Another power is brought 
forth through this sacrifice!

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.950
I activate Savage Destroyer's skill!

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.310
When a Tachikaze unit is put in the drop 
zone, Destroyer's power can increase by +1000!

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.030
This is Tachikaze's fearsomeness!

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:16.270
With this combination play born from 
sacrifice, his attack power escalates in one stroke!

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.260
Certainly, this is amazing!

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:18.710
Oh!

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.950
Exciting, isn't it?!

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:23.010
Indeed!

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.830
It sure is exciting!

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.530
It's because Tachikaze chooses its user...

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:30.730
Hey, you use a Tachikaze deck too, don't you?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.960
Be that as it may, this Jurassic 
Army team is pretty tough...

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.890
So I wonder how our Aichi 
is gonna face him...

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:49.840
Did you see, boy? My Blastsaurus was sacrificed,
 paving the way for the rest of my army.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.450
A path that leads directly to victory!

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.110
Blastsaurus! Take aim at Blaster Blade!

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:00.030
Prepare to mow the enemy down!

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:01.920
Fire!

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:14.590
Damage check!

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:19.910
Yikes! He's got 5 damage!

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:21.130
Checkmate...?!

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.150
Aichi...

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.140
He's strong...

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:25.780
This is the level of nationals...

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.110
This is the national tournament...

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.410
With a boost from Tiny Rex...

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:34.210
Savage Destroyer attacks!

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.550
Oh, no!

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.210
I won't let you do any more damage!

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.720
That marks the end of my engagement.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:00.450
Yeesh! He's got me on pins and needles!

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.010
Yeah. Somehow, he survived that.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:04.500
He's not out of the woods yet.

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:09.190
That's right... Coming up 
is the moment of truth...

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.160
Brother has 5 damage...

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:17.490
He <i>has</i> to win in the next turn!

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.500
And for that, he needs to do 3 damage...

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:25.210
But the other guy is no easy mark...

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.700
If he succeeds in guarding, even once...

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:31.530
Brother will...

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:33.900
Lose this fight!

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:37.040
What should I do?

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:41.270
If my attacks don't get 
through this turn, I...

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:47.260
I can't fight alongside him anymore.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:50.180
So I... I'm sorry!

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:55.170
Right now, instead of chasing after him, 
maybe you should get through the preliminaries...

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:58.020
And secure a place for him to come back to.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:00.210
Kamui...

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:04.370
But... I'm not throwing in the towel yet.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:08.080
I've decided that I'm gonna win this match!

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.210
No matter what the odds are...

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.560
I'm <i>not</i> giving up!

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:18.340
All right, we've got Team Jurassic 
Army versus Team Quadrafolio!

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:22.730
It's been a fierce battle between the first 
Fighters, but the conclusion is in sight!

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.140
Am I right?

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:25.470
Yes, indeed.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:28.340
If Aichi Sendou of Team Q4...

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:32.220
can deliver 3 points of damage 
to Ryudou during this turn...

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.270
3 damage?

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:36.320
That's a tall order, isn't it?

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.370
Exactly.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.240
You understand well.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:45.000
In the first place, by most definitions, 
doing 3 damage this turn would be impossible.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.080
If you state that definitely...

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:49.930
There'd be no fun in that!

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:53.640
Not knowing how it's going to turn out 
is what a Vanguard Fight is about!

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.700
Let's hope for a miracle.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.510
You're absolutely right-o!

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.350
Both of you, do your best!

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:01.790
I stand and draw!

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.900
Come forth, holy dragon!

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:16.880
And wield your mystic power!

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:20.030
I ride Soulsaver Dragon!

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.690
Soulsaver Dragon, eh?

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:31.130
You brought out your ultimate 
weapon, didn't you, boy?

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:32.770
I call Wingal!

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:36.050
Right now, I've got my strongest lineup.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.890
We'll do our best together!

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:43.730
With a boost from Marron...

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:45.870
Gordon attacks Deathrex!

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.770
I defend with Black Cannon Tiger!

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.360
He blocked it!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.320
Is this the end?

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:05.370
Not yet!

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:08.200
I'm not giving up!

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:10.370
With Barcgal's boost...

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.270
Soulsaver Dragon attacks!

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:21.420
It's like you can see your 
defeat... You're a brave boy...

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:24.560
I activate Soulsaver Dragon's skill!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:32.350
When Soulsaver Dragon attacks a Vanguard, 
his power increases by +3000!

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.580
Twin drive, first check!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.520
Second check!

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:44.990
Epona...

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.790
Critical trigger!

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.750
He can do 2 damage at once like this!

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:55.850
If it works out, he may even be 
able to do 3 damage this turn!

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:58.880
What is this?! A miracle?!

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:00.960
I got a trigger!

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:03.410
I add +5000 to the power of Morgana!

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:04.950
And then...

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:08.100
I give the extra critical 
to Soulsaver Dragon!

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:13.520
Damage trigger...

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:14.780
One!

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.270
Two!

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.660
Yes!! Now Aichi's just one step away, too!

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.650
1 more...

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.210
I have to get through this 
turn, no matter what!

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.960
This soldier's shield is 10000...

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.480
What's the boy's attacking strength?!

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:40.510
The enemy has a total of 17000...

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.480
My army has 20000...

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:46.180
I can defend!

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:47.950
With a boost from Wingal...

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:50.180
Morgana attacks Deathrex!

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:53.690
And then I activate Morgana's skill!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:59.130
If I discard one unit from my 
hand, Morgana's power is +4000!

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:00.190
Darn it!

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:04.570
I was careless!

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:07.840
I made a huge tactical error...

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:09.990
Here I go!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:42.500
All right!!

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.230
Aichi's gonna win!

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:47.910
He really did do 3 damage this turn...

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.760
That's amazing, Brother!

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:09.890
He hasn't given up yet!

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.430
Damage check!

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:19.160
I activate a heal trigger!

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.140
I don't believe it...

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:30.000
I heal 1 point of damage!

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.400
I... I didn't think...

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:37.710
I'm done.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.880
All right, time to move to my final attack!

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:46.630
Right now, I only have two 
cards to defend with...

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:48.770
1 damage is inevitable...

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.220
What should I do?!

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:52.720
He can only declare: "no guard".

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.890
There're no other options left.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:58.940
If he's going to lose anyway,

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.060
all he can do is let himself take damage,

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:04.050
and bet on a trigger coming up.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.820
Skyptero gives a boost!

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.410
Blastsaurus...

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.910
Attack Soulsaver Dragon!

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.620
No guard!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.880
You're accepting this with good grace, boy!

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:32.100
Damage check.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:56.380
The winner, Gunji Ryudou!

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:04.360
That first match was important...

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.790
It was a fight that I had to win...

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:10.970
Well, that was a marvelous fight!

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.690
It was a series of miracles, wasn't it?

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:16.710
This is why I can't quit Vanguard!

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:20.550
Let's give a big round of applause 
to both of the Fighters!

00:15:30.770 --> 00:15:33.820
Captain, that was a splendid victory.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.350
Don't underestimate Team Q4.

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:40.420
If their other Fighters are like him, 
they'll have considerable strength.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:46.810
Don't get discouraged.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:51.760
If I win, next in line is Kai, right?

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.050
Misaki...

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.900
Well, it's my turn.

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:58.140
I'm going to go all out, 
no less than you did.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:15:59.760
Right!

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:03.190
Misaki, we're counting on you!

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.590
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.650
Godhawk, Ichibyoshi!

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:17.520
In this second match, it's Bunji 
Ryugawa versus Misaki Tokura.

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:20.840
This technical fight is also exciting!

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:22.160
My heart's pounding!

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:24.710
Please, Misaki...

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:26.380
Jeez...

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:30.380
I've never bothered watching a 
match in another block before.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:34.180
Well, it's obvious Ren isn't going to 
appear during the elimination round.

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.930
So I wonder how A Block is...

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.010
Isn't that...

00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:41.640
Team Q4?

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:45.070
Red crystal, illuminate the future.

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:47.480
I ride Scarlet Witch, Coco!

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:56.880
Going by how he's played up 'til now...

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:59.610
the two cards in his hand 
should both be grade 0...

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.110
Wiseman exits the field!

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:05.120
I call Silent Tom and Dream Eater!

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.780
A second Silent Tom!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:14.580
My grade 0 cards are blocked off!

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.540
Her opponent has 4 damage now...

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:19.320
And Misaki has 5...

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:21.140
If she doesn't settle it here...

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.930
With a boost from Battle Sister, Chocolat...

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:25.690
I attack Deathrex!

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:36.780
I guard with Black Cannon Tiger and Tiny Rex!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.530
Twin drive...

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:42.900
First check!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.910
Second check!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:52.130
With a boost from Dream Eater...

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:54.020
I attack with Silent Tom!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.110
Damage trigger check!

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:03.920
Yesss!

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:04.970
Just 1 more!

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:05.930
Yeah!

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.370
This is my last one.

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:08.560
With a boost from Gemini...

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:10.020
Silent Tom...

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:14.920
All right!

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:18.030
Damage trigger check!

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:24.950
I heal 1 point of damage!

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:32.380
Oh, no...

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:36.400
It's the same as with Aichi's match!

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:39.090
I-Is this possible?!

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.680
He's attacking...

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.190
Here I go!

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:46.900
Blastsaurus, boosted by Sparksaurus...

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:48.390
attacks Coco!

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:03.400
The winner of the second 
match, Bunji Ryugawa!

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:08.000
In this first fight, the 
winning team is Jurassic Army!

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:15.580
This is...

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.620
This is the national tournament...

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:28.420
Looks like Team Q4 are lightweights, too.

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:30.890
This is their level after all.

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:33.380
They're not our enemies.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:49.780
I'm sorry, Shin.

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:53.120
I had him cornered, but at 
the eleventh hour, he...

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:54.330
Me too...

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:59.630
I guess I'm not strong enough to 
beat a national-level Fighter...

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.840
That's not true.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:05.850
Aichi and Misaki, the same development 
occurred at the end of both your matches.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:08.340
Why do you think that is?

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:14.530
Fights at the national tournament are close 
battles between very strong opponents.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:15.850
In other words...

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:20.440
You and your opponent drive each 
other to the edge of a cliff.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:28.040
Not just one side is pushed to the edge.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:30.500
Both people are.

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:34.250
And when both sides are in that situation,

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:38.190
the slightest imbalance is fatal.

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:42.690
That's right. For example, even 
the blowing of a light breeze...

00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:59.850
You might as well call a breeze 
at that juncture "luck".

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:04.690
Drawing a heal trigger at the 
eleventh hour was their good luck.

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:07.650
However, you could also say this...

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:10.910
If the match was swayed by luck,

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:16.970
it means that both of you contended with 
national level veterans with equal ability.

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:20.650
You should be proud of this.

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:23.380
Shin...

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:27.010
"Manager", right?

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:27.860
Boy!

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:32.210
Aichi Sendou and Misaki Tokura...

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:33.230
We salute you!

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:37.640
Remember this.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:41.320
My army only salutes opponents that 
we deem to be formidable rivals.

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:44.690
Let's meet on the battlefield again someday.

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:50.190
They recognize your strength, too.

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:52.900
And there are still two fights left.

00:21:52.900 --> 00:21:55.150
Let's do our best in the next fight.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:55.980
Okay!

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:07.350
That was A Block's first fight, 
a fabulous tension-filled treat.

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:10.470
But we're just getting started!

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:14.800
So winning Fighters and losing Fighters, 
prepare for your next fight!

00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:17.710
Come on, let's form an image!

00:23:52.820 --> 00:23:55.660
I fought with everything I had, but...

00:23:55.660 --> 00:23:58.240
I figured out which cards my 
opponent had in his hand...

00:23:58.240 --> 00:24:01.770
That's what's scary about the national 
tournament, but it's also fun.

00:24:01.770 --> 00:24:02.990
If you feel that down about it,

00:24:02.990 --> 00:24:05.780
the people who couldn't come are going 
to get mad at you for asking too much.

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:06.460
I see...

00:24:06.700 --> 00:24:09.940
We won the shop tournament and now 
we're here as representatives.

00:24:09.940 --> 00:24:12.020
Let's win, laugh, and go home!

00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:14.540
Next: When the Moon is Full

00:24:14.540 --> 00:24:17.900
My father's card will 
become whatever I imagine!
